g to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\nSolving for $u$, we have $u(x) =$ {{field-2}}.\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is $y_{p}(x) =$ {{field-3}}."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f679671-78d2-5511-aa7e-99b1b7f04889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\displaystyle\\int e^{-2x}\\cos 4x\\" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155392} {:answer/id #uuid "96fe4bea-8d41-5153-8d23-c1ee5a2eac0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "\\textrm d x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155393} {:answer/id #uuid "c09833b1-593a-5e42-a92e-1e7c8c4ca0c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\displaystyle\\int e^{2x}\\cos 4x\\" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155394} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b36537-e7f2-58da-9b29-99024366cb50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\displaystyle\\int e^{-2x}\\sin 4x\\" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155395} {:answer/id #uuid "5f880e36-8f81-5c27-a1c8-13a569b241dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\displaystyle\\int e^{2x}\\sin 4x\\" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155396}] :answer-field/id #uuid "cacdf1b8-748c-5cea-96a1-16ccf26ab940" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155391} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91dcfc07-49d0-5122-94a9-06c35d2d5b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{− 4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155398} {:answer/id #uuid "94a59549-1a48-59f2-802c-2646623d7440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155399} {:answer/id #uuid "9d534a6e-134a-5e12-96a0-1cfcdb092423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "