ding to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\nSolving for $u$, we have $u(x) =$ {{field-2}}.\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is $y_{p}(x) =$ {{field-3}}."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using VOP When the Forcing Term is Part of the Complementary Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1034da1-ae39-5071-beb9-d524c91b3460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155428} {:answer/id #uuid "ad718114-0514-5c21-9296-0a1cb9a1d0bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{− 4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155429} {:answer/id #uuid "f723a595-68b1-5b1c-b418-3f893ec254a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155430} {:answer/id #uuid "ff834ebb-28f4-5f0e-adbb-4ac4dc78a4be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{− 2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155431} {:answer/id #uuid "1e6783e9-23fd-51be-9ee6-57060434f79f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155432}] :answer-field/id #uuid "05ea8b44-cc8a-5121-9427-a141af1d5b6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155427} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2eeb174-374e-5dde-a1f7-1f6c1c0574dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2x} − xe^{− 2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155434} {:answer/id #uuid "bad49942-1371-5682-ac55-d9bceb478c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xe^{2x} − (1)/(2)e^{− 2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155435} {:answer/id #uuid "4027305d-c9ab-54aa-922c-545cbd7965cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2x} − (1)/(2)xe^{− 2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 1